{"4853620": {"success": true, "data": {"type": "game", "name": "Verdantis", "steam_appid": 4853620, "required_age": 0, "is_free": false, "controller_support": "full", "detailed_description": "<h2 class=\"bb_tag\" ><strong>Verdantis begins in the soil</strong></h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><img class=\"bb_img\" src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/4853620/extras/6ab9098d8298646c2679b13588c83576.avif?t=1783675829\" data-big-src=https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/4853620/extras_big/6ab9098d8298646c2679b13588c83576.avif?t=1783675829 width=1560 height=878 /></span></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong><i>Verdantis</i></strong> is a puzzle-adventure game, set in a ruined, overgrown research facility. Once a cutting-edge complex for alternative energy experiments. Today vines, and rust reclaim the laboratories, and reactors.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >You play as R-0B, a small quadruped assistant robot. Your task: restore power across the entire complex, zone by zone, puzzle by puzzle. The story unfolds through exploration, researchers' journal entries, and traces of disaster in the environment.</p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" ><strong>Mechanics</strong></h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><img class=\"bb_img\" src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/4853620/extras/e9546e45cefbe2db8900909c8cd06bf8.avif?t=1783675829\" width=1080 height=830 /></span></p><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Block pushing</strong> – push blocks and plan your movement through tight, logical spaces</p></li></ul><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Switches and activators</strong> – open doors, route power, and trigger devices, no time pressure</p></li></ul><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Electric charges</strong> – take on a positive or negative charge and manipulate plants</p></li></ul><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Floating plants</strong> – cross flooded labs where vegetation responds to energy</p></li></ul><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Light reflection</strong> – guide beams through light-reflecting plants to trigger reactions in other plants and create platforms</p></li></ul><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>And more</strong></p></li></ul><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >The world is split into eight connected zones: from industrial ruins to dense vegetation at the heart of the facility. You can explore the facility in any order.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >The game offers about 2 hours of play time. Progress saves automatically.</p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" ><strong>Visual style</strong></h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><img class=\"bb_img\" src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/4853620/extras/bb5588c0082a4e32d84fc56d468379a7.avif?t=1783675829\" data-big-src=https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/4853620/extras_big/bb5588c0082a4e32d84fc56d468379a7.avif?t=1783675829 width=1560 height=878 /></span></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Verdantis stands out with a distinctive look: cel-shading with bold outlines, comic-book readability, and post-apocalyptic technology overtaken by nature. Rusted machines, dense overgrowth, and gradually returning light create the mood of an abandoned lab slowly coming back to life.</p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" ><strong>Who is it for?</strong></h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >For players who want a calm adventure built on logic and exploration with a readable world, consistent puzzles, and a strong, original visual identity.</p>", "about_the_game": "<h2 class=\"bb_tag\" ><strong>Verdantis begins in the soil</strong></h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><img class=\"bb_img\" src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/4853620/extras/6ab9098d8298646c2679b13588c83576.avif?t=1783675829\" data-big-src=https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/4853620/extras_big/6ab9098d8298646c2679b13588c83576.avif?t=1783675829 width=1560 height=878 /></span></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong><i>Verdantis</i></strong> is a puzzle-adventure game, set in a ruined, overgrown research facility. Once a cutting-edge complex for alternative energy experiments. Today vines, and rust reclaim the laboratories, and reactors.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >You play as R-0B, a small quadruped assistant robot. Your task: restore power across the entire complex, zone by zone, puzzle by puzzle. The story unfolds through exploration, researchers' journal entries, and traces of disaster in the environment.</p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" ><strong>Mechanics</strong></h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><img class=\"bb_img\" src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/4853620/extras/e9546e45cefbe2db8900909c8cd06bf8.avif?t=1783675829\" width=1080 height=830 /></span></p><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Block pushing</strong> – push blocks and plan your movement through tight, logical spaces</p></li></ul><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Switches and activators</strong> – open doors, route power, and trigger devices, no time pressure</p></li></ul><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Electric charges</strong> – take on a positive or negative charge and manipulate plants</p></li></ul><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Floating plants</strong> – cross flooded labs where vegetation responds to energy</p></li></ul><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Light reflection</strong> – guide beams through light-reflecting plants to trigger reactions in other plants and create platforms</p></li></ul><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>And more</strong></p></li></ul><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >The world is split into eight connected zones: from industrial ruins to dense vegetation at the heart of the facility. You can explore the facility in any order.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >The game offers about 2 hours of play time. Progress saves automatically.</p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" ><strong>Visual style</strong></h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><img class=\"bb_img\" src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/4853620/extras/bb5588c0082a4e32d84fc56d468379a7.avif?t=1783675829\" data-big-src=https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/4853620/extras_big/bb5588c0082a4e32d84fc56d468379a7.avif?t=1783675829 width=1560 height=878 /></span></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Verdantis stands out with a distinctive look: cel-shading with bold outlines, comic-book readability, and post-apocalyptic technology overtaken by nature. Rusted machines, dense overgrowth, and gradually returning light create the mood of an abandoned lab slowly coming back to life.</p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" ><strong>Who is it for?</strong></h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >For players who want a calm adventure built on logic and exploration with a readable world, consistent puzzles, and a strong, original visual identity.</p>", "short_description": "Verdantis begins in the soil. Play as R-0B and restore power in an overgrown research facility. Cel-shading, chloropunk, and environmental puzzles. The game offers about 2 hours of play.", "supported_languages": "English<strong>*</strong>, German, Spanish - Spain, Polish, Simplified Chinese<br><strong>*</strong>languages with full audio support", "header_image": "https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/4853620/4f1286dac902835c5a86b9ede188012a5c619b0b/header.jpg?t=1783675829", "capsule_image": "https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/4853620/a1ac55e7bbea20c58bd92bd2